WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.320
Movie the Deception of the Photon

00:03.060 --> 00:06.200
Imagine walking into a room where a game of hide-and-seek is going on

00:06.400 --> 00:13.220
There's a chameleon a master of disguise that either shows up as a wave or a particle. It's a bizarre game, isn't it?

00:13.400 --> 00:20.360
But that's precisely what we encounter in the world of quantum physics here light our omnipresent chameleon

00:20.520 --> 00:22.520
Plays a fascinating game of hide-and-seek

00:23.080 --> 00:29.020
Sometimes appearing as a wave undulating and spreading and at other times showing up as a particle

00:29.340 --> 00:34.780
Discreet and localized. It's a mysterious duality that has puzzled scientists for centuries

00:34.860 --> 00:38.580
Just when you think you've got it figured out the chameleon changes its form

00:39.100 --> 00:42.980
Confounding expectations and challenging our understanding of the physical world

00:43.340 --> 00:46.940
It's the enigma of light a paradox that continues to intrigue us

00:47.100 --> 00:52.380
This chameleon my friends is not a creature of the wild but rather it's light itself

00:52.660 --> 00:58.100
To understand this chameleon better scientists conducted an experiment known as the double slit experiment

00:58.460 --> 01:04.840
This is where the intriguing behavior of light comes to the fore where it plays the roles of both a particle and a wave

01:05.300 --> 01:07.020
Keeping us on our toes

01:07.020 --> 01:11.540
Imagine light as a stream of tiny particles or photons passing through one slit

01:11.540 --> 01:18.820
You'd expect them to form a single band of light on the screen behind now introduce a second slit if light were purely particle-like

01:19.060 --> 01:23.200
You'd expect two bright bands on the screen each corresponding to a slit

01:23.480 --> 01:29.760
But that's not what you see instead you see a pattern of alternating light and dark bands known as an interference pattern

01:29.760 --> 01:33.040
This is something you'd expect from waves not particles

01:33.480 --> 01:37.080
Picture throwing two stones in a compound the ripples

01:37.080 --> 01:42.240
They create will intersect making some areas with bigger waves and some with no waves at all

01:42.560 --> 01:47.280
This is exactly the pattern we see in the double slit experiment when light is unobserved

01:48.040 --> 01:49.660
Suggesting it behaves like a wave

01:49.660 --> 01:56.740
But here's the twist when we place detectors near the slits to observe which one the photon passes through the

01:56.940 --> 02:01.860
Interference pattern disappears instead. We get two bands of light just like we'd expect from particles

02:01.860 --> 02:05.940
It's as if the light knows it's being watched and decides to behave like particles

02:05.940 --> 02:11.380
in essence the double slit experiment revealed that light can behave as both a wave and a particle a

02:11.740 --> 02:18.520
Concept known as wave particle duality. It's one of the most fascinating and perplexing outcomes in the world of quantum physics

02:19.200 --> 02:21.760
Challenging our understanding of the nature of reality

02:21.760 --> 02:27.760
So the light decided to behave as a wave or a particle based on whether we were watching a perfect hide-and-seek game

02:27.760 --> 02:34.880
Isn't it the enigma of light continues to baffle us and the double slit experiment is a perfect example of this tantalizing mystery

02:35.120 --> 02:38.760
But how can something be both a wave and a particle at the same time?

02:39.160 --> 02:42.760
Welcome to the photon deception in this mesmerizing dance of nature

02:43.240 --> 02:47.240
Light twirls around with the grace of a wave and the precision of a particle

02:47.560 --> 02:50.200
This is the concept of wave particle duality

02:50.360 --> 02:55.360
It's not that light is sometimes a wave and sometimes a particle but rather that it is always both

02:55.840 --> 03:01.760
The secret lies in photons the fundamental building blocks of light photons are peculiar to say the least

03:01.800 --> 03:05.580
They are particles with zero mass, but they carry energy and momentum now

03:05.580 --> 03:09.060
Here's the twist these massless particles can also behave like waves

03:09.060 --> 03:15.840
They can interfere with each other creating patterns of light and dark just like waves on a pond in the double slit experiment

03:15.840 --> 03:22.060
Photons pass through two slits and create an interference pattern on a screen a behavior characteristic of waves not particles

03:22.320 --> 03:28.020
Yet when we measure photons, they seem to hit the screen like tiny particles not spread out like waves

03:28.360 --> 03:34.160
This is the heart of the photon deception when left to their own devices photons behave like waves

03:34.440 --> 03:39.980
But when we try to pin them down they act like particles. It's as if they know when we're watching

03:40.040 --> 03:42.040
This is one of the most mind-boggling

03:42.300 --> 03:49.380
Aspects of quantum physics the mere act of observing can change the outcome of an experiment the observer effect as it's known

03:49.860 --> 03:56.020
Tells us that the very act of watching can change the nature of reality. So here we are caught in the photon deception

03:56.260 --> 03:59.300
How can something be both a wave and a particle at the same time?

03:59.300 --> 04:05.820
the answer it seems is hidden in the strange counterintuitive world of quantum physics a world where particles can be in two places at

04:05.820 --> 04:10.940
Once where reality changes when you look at it and where light is both a wave and a particle and

04:11.580 --> 04:14.180
So the chameleon continues to baffle us

04:14.640 --> 04:19.920
Existing as both a wave and a particle forever keeping us on a thrilling chase in the game of quantum physics

